# Commit / push copy (RELEASE.md §8)

When the user says 提交 / 推送 / push, **read `RELEASE.md` §8 first** and write the message **before** `git commit`. Do not use a one-line or 1–2 sentence body. The generic “concise commit” habit does **not** apply in this repo.

## Git commits (feat / fix / chore / docs / test)

Title: `type: 一句话摘要` (release commits use `release: comm-vX.Y.Z — …`).

Body **must** be numbered sections with `-` bullets, blank line between sections:

```
feat: 多会话引擎按标签独立运行

1. 脚本 / MBM / 序列
- 双标签可各跑；Run/Stop 跟当前标签
- 关控制台结束全部 worker

2. 测试
- …

全量测试：1594 passed，11 skipped，295 subtests passed。
```

Include: what landed, user-visible behavior, compatibility, docs, tests. End with **full** pytest numbers when a suite was run. Confirm with `git log -1 --format='%B'` before push.

## Releases

Same body depth for GitHub/Gitee Release. Current version only; do not paste older versions into this Release.

## Forbidden

- Title-only, or title + one paragraph of joined clauses
- Dropping section bullets to “save space”
- Amending a detailed message into a short one
- PowerShell `git commit -m "…"` for Chinese bodies (encoding breaks). Write UTF-8 file, then `git commit -F` that file.
